# Rules for Prompts 11 onward (read before every prompt)

Prompts 0 to 10 are Phase 1. From Prompt 11 (Vendors and purchases) every prompt must follow this contract. Paste the contract from `docs/PROMPTS.md` (“Contract for Prompts 11 onward”) at the top of each new Cursor chat, or keep this file with `alwaysApply: true`.

Build only what the prompt lists, with sources in Spec / Arch / Roadmap / PDF. Do not invent pages, tables, counters or integrations. If something useful is missing from the documents, list it at the end — do not build it.

## Prompt 11 onward contract

**A. Decide the surface before writing code.**
Follow `ui-flows.mdc` (User goal, Flow map, Entry and exit points). Add one more table: for every record type the user will look for later (vendor, purchase order, appointment, expense, and so on), list its own route, list page, detail page, create/edit page, nav entry and allowed roles. A record type that owners look for later gets its own pages and nav entry — not only a section inside a job card (a job card section may link to the real page). Show this and **wait for confirmation before building**.

**B. Build only the listed items.**
No pages, tables, settings, reports, PDFs, counters or integrations that are not in the prompt. Ask which provider to use before adding WhatsApp, SMS, AI or barcode libraries.

**C. Build real things only.**
No stubs, no placeholder data, no buttons that only copy a link. Anything that sends a message must really send in development and write a log row. If a provider key is missing, show a clear setup message in Settings, never a fake success.

**D. UI and project rules.**
Follow `.cursor/rules/ui-flows.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/garage.mdc`. Layering, `garageId` from session, integer paise, stock only through `StockMovement` in a transaction, audit log, Zod, en/hi/gu, loading/empty/error, 360px to desktop.

**E. Proof.**
Vitest for business rules named in the prompt. For stock, money, numbering and concurrency: use the **same local Postgres** as the app (`DATABASE_URL` / docker-compose) — real Prisma, not mocks. No separate test database. Garage-isolation test for every new table. One Playwright test for the main flow starting from the nav.

**F. Finish with.**
Done when checklist (Done / Partial / Missing, file path and test name), what remains, and `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`.

Do not start the next prompt. Do not refactor unrelated code.
